# Boundary policy record: Swift ordinary read-only array boundary

Status: DRAFT for independent review. Revision-specific: all code citations are
against the coordination tree working copy (HEAD `e1c65975` plus uncommitted
applied edits). Produced per the architectural instruction that the next move is
to ACCEPT A BOUNDARY POLICY RECORD rather than repair another symptom.

## 1. Source semantic ruling and accepted input domain

The boundary exists when a Haxe array value crosses into a Swift position whose
destination storage differs from the source storage. The source-side meaning is
carried by `SwiftArrayStorage`; the destination requirement is carried by the
destination type at the consuming position.

Accepted input domain for this record: ordinary read-only arrays and their
optional and literal forms, at positions enumerated in section 4.

